  "step1_summary": "• Chief complaint: Painful, itchy, cracked, very dry skin on palms of both hands for 3–4 months.\n• Symptom details: Began shortly after starting a new housekeeping job; worsened progressively and now ‘hurts a lot’ and forced 3 days off work. Occasional bleeding only after scratching. Itch intermittent. Mild generalized xerosis on legs. No fever, GI, GU, or systemic symptoms.\n• Past medical history: Type 2 diabetes mellitus.\n• Medications/Allergies: Metformin 500 mg (dose not specified). Tried OTC E45 emollient and an antihistamine without benefit. No known drug or other allergies.\n• Family history: Diabetes; no known dermatologic, asthma, or bowel disease.\n• Social history: Hotel housekeeper; frequent exposure to cleaning chemicals; often does not wear gloves. Non-smoker. Alcohol: ~2 pints beer/week.\n• Vital signs / physical exam: None provided (tele-visit). Patient reports marked palmar dryness, fissuring, cracking; no spontaneous bleeding; occasional itch.\n• Labs/Imaging: None mentioned.",
